;; ============================================================================

;; MEMORY SSA  —  port of Simple's MemOpNode, LoadNode, StoreNode, NewNode,
;;                MemMergeNode, MemPhiNode, ReadOnlyNode
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; ## Memory is not one value
;;
;; It is split into ALIAS CLASSES — one per field of one shape — and each class is threaded through
;; the graph as its own SSA edge. That is the whole idea, and it is what turns load-after-store
;; forwarding from an ANALYSIS into a PEEPHOLE: a Load reads the Store that most recently wrote ITS
;; class, and finding that Store is following one edge.
;;
;; Simple's `LoadNode.idealize` says it outright: "Equiv class aliasing is perfect" — when a Load's
;; memory input IS a Store on the same pointer and offset, the alias classes agreeing is enough to
;; assert the field names agree. That precision is the payoff.
;;
;; ## Where the alias classes come from  (src/shape.coil)
;;
;; A field's alias class and byte offset are allocated at the shape-transition edge that INTRODUCES
;; the field, and inherited unchanged by every descendant. A store through `{x}` and a load through
;; `{x,y}` therefore name the same word, because `{x,y}` was reached FROM `{x}` and a transition
;; never moves an existing field.
;;
;; Allocate per-shape-per-field instead and those two touch different words, so forwarding silently
;; stops firing. No error, no crash — just worse code, which is the hardest kind of bug to notice.
;;
;; ## Load: the peepholes, in Simple's order
;;
;; 1. DROP THE CONTROL EDGE. A load from a struct needs no control, because null-pointer checking is
;;    in the TYPE SYSTEM rather than in a runtime test. A load from an ARRAY keeps its control edge
;;    until range checking exists. Control-free loads float, which is what lets GCM hoist them.
;;
;; 2. SHARPEN THE ALIAS. In final Simple, a forward-referenced pointer eventually exposes the
;;    declaring Field and `LoadNode.idealize` adopts its alias after `unlock()`, because the alias is
;;    part of GVN identity. Here hidden-class lowering already supplies the transition's alias to
;;    `load-make`; a producer that begins at bulk alias must call `load-sharpen-alias!`, which applies
;;    the same unlock-and-requeue protocol. The idealizer does not infer a ShapeTable field name.
;;
;;    Everything after this point is guarded on `_alias != 1` — the bulk "all memory" alias must be
;;    sharpened before any forwarding is legal.
;;
;; 3. LOAD-AFTER-STORE, same address. Memory input is a Store on the same pointer and offset ->
;;    become the stored value.
;;
;; 4. NORMALISE THE MEMORY INPUT to the effective one `compute` already looked through, re-queueing
;;    the other loads on that memory so they get the same chance.
;;
;; 5. UPLIFT TO A DOMINATING LOAD. If another Load has the same memory, pointer and offset but
;;    HIGHER control — checked with `_idom` — become it. This is CSE across control flow, done with
;;    a dominator query rather than a value-numbering pass.
;;
;; 6. LOAD-AFTER-STORE BYPASSING UNRELATED STORES. Final Simple walks through pointer/offset-proven
;;    non-aliasing stores, calls, projections, merges and escape boundaries. This implementation
;;    currently performs only the sound precise-slice case: an immediately preceding Store with a
;;    different alias is bypassed. The broader walk is intentionally not claimed here.
;;
;; ## THE POINTER RULE  (verifier: VERR-PTR-SLOT)
;;
;; A Load or Store's pointer operand must be an object and NOTHING ELSE. Not "could be an object":
;; address arithmetic types as plain `dyn`, and `dyn` INCLUDES objects, so the weaker test admits
;; exactly the interior pointers the GC contract exists to keep out of the graph.
;;
;; A value that is honestly `dyn` at a memory access needs a Cast to object first — the same shape
;; every other narrowing has (src/node/dynamic.coil). The verifier ABSTAINS while the pointer's type
;; is high, which is the same optimistic case `load-compute` special-cases.
;;
;; Two related checks are deliberately NOT verifier rules: "the memory state carries the class this
;; node names" and "the pointer's shape carries this word". Both are unions over paths, so a state
;; that statically carries a class need not carry it on the path actually taken. They belong to the
;; interpreter (EV-MEM, EV-SHAPE). What the compiler owes instead is that no REWRITE launders such
;; an access into a plausible value.
;;
;; ## MemMerge and MemPhi
;;
;; MEMMERGE is the bundle of per-class memory edges that a call or a merge passes around whole —
;; you cannot hand a callee "memory" without naming every class.
;;
;; MEMPHI is an ordinary Phi over a memory edge, carrying an alias class (see src/node/phi.coil).
;; It matters that it is the SAME node kind: every Phi rule then applies to memory merges with no
;; second implementation to keep in agreement. `BulkMemPhi` is the alias-1 case.
;;
;; NEW follows final Simple's two-result boundary: a fresh pointer and its private initial bulk
;; memory. Field initialization splits that private state into precise aliases as stores are built;
;; allocation does not pretend those stores already happened.
;;
;; READONLY is presently an idempotent graph marker used by memory and target code. Final Simple
;; also feeds its deep-read-only type into Store diagnostics; this frontend does not yet construct
;; object stores, so that source diagnostic is not implemented in this module.
;;
;; ## The trait boundary
;;
;; Simple has `MemOpNode` as a shared base for Load and Store, carrying the alias, the field name
;; and the `_isLoad` flag. `MemOps` below is that base. GCM's anti-dependence walk asks exactly
;; these questions — "are you a load", "which alias" — and asks nothing else.
;;
;; STATUS: implemented for the current object-memory boundary: precise Load/Store types and basic
;; forwarding, sparse MemMerge selection/collapse, MemPhi construction, fresh New projection types,
;; ReadOnly identity, and the target-neutral MemOps query used by GCM. The missing final-Simple
;; alias-inference and broad unrelated-store walk are stated above instead of hidden behind a stale
;; scaffold claim.
(module aot.node.memory)
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc :use [unwrap-ptr create box!])
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.control" :use *)
(import "aot.node.constant" :use *)
(import "aot.node.phi" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)
(import "aot.shape" :use *)

;; The bulk "all memory" alias. Nothing may be forwarded through it; a Load must sharpen first.
(const ALIAS-BULK 1)

;; Simple's `MemOpNode`: what Load and Store have in common, and all that GCM's anti-dependence
;; walk needs to ask.
(deftrait MemOps [Self]
  (mem-node [(self (ptr Self))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)))
  ;; Which alias class this access names.
  (mem-alias [(self (ptr Self))] (-> i64))
  ;; Load or Store. GCM orders a Load against every Store on the same alias.
  (mem-is-load? [(self (ptr Self))] (-> bool))
  ;; The memory edge this access reads.
  (mem-in [(self (ptr Self))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)))
  ;; The pointer operand — which must be an object and nothing else.
  (mem-ptr [(self (ptr Self))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)))
  ;; Byte offset within the object. It remains an integer value, not an interior pointer; the
  ;; machine selector folds it into the address mode without exposing a managed interior address.
  (mem-offset [(self (ptr Self))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))))

(const MEM-CTRL 0)

(const MEM-STATE 1)

(const MEM-PTR 2)

(const MEM-OFF 3)

(const STORE-VAL 4)

(defstruct LoadNode [(hdr NodeHdr) (alias i64) (declared i64)])

(defstruct StoreNode [(hdr NodeHdr) (alias i64) (declared i64)])

(defstruct NewNode [(hdr NodeHdr) (shape i64) (object-ty i64)])

(defstruct MemMergeNode [(hdr NodeHdr) (in-progress bool)])

(defstruct ReadOnlyNode [(hdr NodeHdr) (pad i64)])

;; Target ports register the one downcast needed for selected memory nodes. Keeping the hook here
;; means generic GCM continues to consume MemOps without importing a CPU module or switching on a
;; target-specific struct. It is installed before the first selected memory node is returned.
(defstruct SelectedMemHook
  [(get (fnptr c [(ref (dyn NodeOps))] (Option (dyn MemOps))))
   (set bool)])

(defn selected-mem-hook [] (-> (ptr SelectedMemHook))
  (primitive/alloc-static SelectedMemHook))

(defn set-selected-mem-hook! [(get (fnptr c [(ref (dyn NodeOps))] (Option (dyn MemOps))))] (-> i64)
  (do (set! (.get (selected-mem-hook)) get) (set! (.set (selected-mem-hook)) true) 0))

;; The one place that knows which opcodes are memory accesses. Simple's `instanceof MemOpNode`.
(defn mem-of [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn MemOps)))
  (if (= (n-op n) OP-LOAD)
      (Some (primitive/make-dyn MemOps (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr n))))
      (if (= (n-op n) OP-STORE)
          (Some (primitive/make-dyn MemOps (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr n))))
          (if (= (n-op n) OP-MACH-MEM)
              (if (.set (selected-mem-hook))
                  (primitive/call-ptr (.get (selected-mem-hook)) n)
                  (do (panic "mem-of: selected-memory hook is not installed") (None [(dyn MemOps)])))
              (None [(dyn MemOps)])))))

(defn load-declared [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-LOAD)
      (do (panic-i "load-declared: not a Load" (n-op n)) TY-BOT)
      (.declared (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr n)))))

(defn store-declared [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-STORE)
      (do (panic-i "store-declared: not a Store" (n-op n)) TY-BOT)
      (.declared (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr n)))))

(defn mem-alias-of-node [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (mem-of n)
    (Some [m] (mem-alias m))
    (None [] (do (panic-i "mem-alias-of-node: not a memory operation" (n-op n)) ALIAS-BULK))))

(defn mem-effective [(mem (dyn NodeOps)) (alias i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (and (!= alias ALIAS-BULK) (= (n-op mem) OP-MEMMERGE))
      (memmerge-alias mem alias)
      mem))

(defn mem-control-dominates? [(higher (dyn NodeOps)) (lower (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut cur) (Some lower)
        (mut answer) false
        (mut guard) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load guard) 1000000)
              (do (broken "mem-control-dominates?: dominator walk did not converge") (break 0))
              (match (load cur)
                (None [] (break 0))
                (Some [n]
                      (if (n-same? n higher)
                          (do (set! (mut answer) true) (break 0))
                          (do
                            (set! (mut cur) (cfg-idom-of n))
                            (set! (mut guard) (+ (load guard) 1))
                            (continue)))))))
    (load answer)))

(defn load-compute [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [mem (mem-effective (n-in! d MEM-STATE) (.alias (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr d))))
        mt (n-ty mem)
        pt (n-ty (n-in! d MEM-PTR))
        declared (.declared (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr d)))]
    (if (or (ty-high? mt) (ty-high? pt))
        TY-TOP
        (if (not (ty-memptr? pt))
            TY-BOT
            (if (not (ty-mem? mt))
                TY-BOT
                (let [elem (ty-mem-elem mt)
                      slice (mem-effective (n-in! d MEM-STATE) (.alias (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr d))))]
                  ;; A private slice is another object's exact state unless this load reads that
                  ;; very object; then only the declared type is known.
                  (if (and (ty-mem-one? mt) (not (mem-slice-owned-by? slice (n-in! d MEM-PTR))))
                      declared
                      (if (= elem TY-TOP) TY-TOP (ty-join declared elem)))))))))

(defn load-idealize [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [p (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr d))
        alias (.alias p)
        ptr_ (n-in! d MEM-PTR)
        off (n-in! d MEM-OFF)
        raw-mem (n-in! d MEM-STATE)
        mem (mem-effective raw-mem alias)]
    ;; A fresh allocation's runtime header is established by New itself. Exposing that exact shape
    ;; is what collapses JSL's closed-world property dispatch without inventing a second shape
    ;; analysis or teaching the frontend about object layouts.
    (if (and (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-SHAPE)
             (and (= (n-op ptr_) OP-PROJ)
                  (and (= (proj-idx ptr_) 0) (= (n-op (n-in! ptr_ 0)) OP-NEW))))
        (Some (con-int (new-shape (n-in! ptr_ 0))))
    ;; Object accesses do not need control after the pointer type proves an object; nullability is
    ;; discharged before this point by ordinary guard control.
    (if (and (match (n-in d MEM-CTRL) (Some [_] true) (None [] false))
             (ty-memptr? (n-ty ptr_)))
        (do (n-set-def! d MEM-CTRL (None [(dyn NodeOps)])) (Some d))
        (if (not (n-same? mem raw-mem))
            (do (n-set-def! d MEM-STATE (Some mem)) (Some d))
            (if (= alias ALIAS-BULK)
                (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
                (if (= (n-op mem) OP-STORE)
                    (let [st (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr mem))]
                      (if (and (= alias (.alias st))
                               (and (n-same? ptr_ (n-in! mem MEM-PTR))
                                    (n-same? off (n-in! mem MEM-OFF))))
                          (Some (n-in! mem STORE-VAL))
                          ;; Distinct alias slices cannot clobber one another, and neither can a
                          ;; store into a provably different object: two distinct allocations
                          ;; never alias (Simple's Load-after-Store bypass of unrelated stores).
                          (if (or (!= alias (.alias st))
                                  (mem-provably-distinct? ptr_ (n-in! mem MEM-PTR)))
                              (do (n-set-def! d MEM-STATE (Some (n-in! mem MEM-STATE))) (Some d))
                              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))))
                    ;; Uplift to an equivalent load whose control dominates ours.
                    (let [(mut i) 0
                          (mut prior) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])]
                      (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nouts mem))
                                (break 0)
                                (do
                                  (match (n-out mem (load i))
                                    (Some [use]
                                          (if (and (= (n-op use) OP-LOAD)
                                                   (and (not (n-same? use d))
                                                        (and (= (load-alias use) alias)
                                                             (and (n-same? (n-in! use MEM-PTR) ptr_)
                                                                  (n-same? (n-in! use MEM-OFF) off)))))
                                              (match (n-in use MEM-CTRL)
                                                (Some [higher]
                                                      (match (n-in d MEM-CTRL)
                                                        (Some [lower]
                                                              (if (mem-control-dominates? higher lower)
                                                                  (do (set! (mut prior) (Some use)) (break 0))
                                                                  0))
                                                        (None [] 0)))
                                                (None [] (do (set! (mut prior) (Some use)) (break 0))))
                                              0))
                                    (None [] 0))
                                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                  (continue))))
                      (load prior)))))))))

;; Two pointers that are each the result of a different New can never address the same object.
(defn mem-provably-distinct? [(a (dyn NodeOps)) (b (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (and (= (n-op a) OP-PROJ) (= (n-op b) OP-PROJ)
       (= (proj-idx a) 0) (= (proj-idx b) 0)
       (= (n-op (n-in! a 0)) OP-NEW) (= (n-op (n-in! b 0)) OP-NEW)
       (not (n-same? (n-in! a 0) (n-in! b 0)))))

(defn load-alias [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (.alias (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr d))))

(defn load-sharpen-alias! [(ld (dyn NodeOps)) (alias i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op ld) OP-LOAD)
      (panic-i "load-sharpen-alias!: not a Load" (n-op ld))
      (let [p (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr ld))]
        (if (or (= (.alias p) ALIAS-BULK) (= (.alias p) alias))
            (do (n-unlock! ld) (set! (.alias p) alias) (code-add! ld) 0)
            (panic-i "load-sharpen-alias!: conflicting precise alias" alias)))))

(impl NodeOps LoadNode
  (hdr [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (ptr NodeHdr)) (primitive/cast (ptr NodeHdr) self))
  (label [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (slice u8)) "Load")
  (is-const? [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (no-const-fold? [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (is-pinned? [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (binop-copy [(self (ptr LoadNode)) (lhs (dyn NodeOps)) (rhs (dyn NodeOps))]
              (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  (compute [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> i64) (load-compute (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (idealize [(self (ptr LoadNode))]
            (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
            (load-idealize (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (eq-extra [(self (ptr LoadNode)) (other (dyn NodeOps))]
            (-> bool)
            (if (!= (n-op other) OP-LOAD)
                false
                (let [o (primitive/cast (ptr LoadNode) (hdr other))]
                  (and (= (.alias self) (.alias o)) (= (.declared self) (.declared o))))))
  (hash-extra [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> i64) (^ (* (.alias self) 251) (.declared self))))

(impl MemOps LoadNode
  (mem-node [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self))
  (mem-alias [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> i64) (.alias self))
  (mem-is-load? [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (mem-in [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-STATE))
  (mem-ptr [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-PTR))
  (mem-offset [(self (ptr LoadNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-OFF)))

(defn store-compute [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [p (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr d))
        mt (n-ty (mem-effective (n-in! d MEM-STATE) (.alias p)))
        pt (n-ty (n-in! d MEM-PTR))
        vt (n-ty (n-in! d STORE-VAL))]
    (if (or (ty-high? mt) (ty-high? pt) (ty-high? vt))
        (ty-mem-top (.alias p))
        (if (or (not (ty-mem? mt)) (not (ty-memptr? pt)))
            (ty-mem (.alias p) TY-BOT)
            ;; Final Simple: the slice after a store is `val.meet(tfld)`, the stored value MET with
            ;; what the slice already held, because other objects share the alias. An allocation's
            ;; private memory (`mem._one`) is the exception and tracks just the value. Here that
            ;; private state is the New's own bulk slice typed by its struct; a fresh slice with a
            ;; TOP remainder also contributes nothing.
            ;; Final Simple: the slice after a store is `val.meet(tfld)`, the stored value MET with
            ;; what the slice already held, because other objects share the alias. An allocation's
            ;; private memory (`mem._one`) is the exception and tracks just the value. A private
            ;; slice describes ONE object: continuing it for that same object keeps it private and
            ;; exact; a store to any other object cannot use it as a prior at all (BOT), because the
            ;; alias's public state is not what that slice holds.
            (let [sharpened (ty-join (.declared p) vt)
                  prior (ty-mem-elem mt)
                  same-object (mem-slice-owned-by? (mem-effective (n-in! d MEM-STATE) (.alias p)) (n-in! d MEM-PTR))]
              (if (ty-mem-one? mt)
                  (if same-object
                      (ty-mem-private (.alias p) sharpened)
                      (ty-mem (.alias p) TY-BOT))
                  (ty-mem (.alias p) (if (= prior TY-TOP) sharpened (ty-meet sharpened prior)))))))))

;; Whether a memory node is the private state of exactly the object `ptr`: the allocation's own
;; projection, or a store to that same pointer continuing it.
(defn mem-slice-owned-by? [(slice (dyn NodeOps)) (ptr_ (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (if (= (n-op slice) OP-STORE)
      (n-same? (n-in! slice MEM-PTR) ptr_)
      (if (and (= (n-op slice) OP-PROJ) (= (n-op (n-in! slice 0)) OP-NEW))
          (and (= (n-op ptr_) OP-PROJ) (n-same? (n-in! ptr_ 0) (n-in! slice 0)))
          false)))

(defn store-idealize [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [p (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr d))
        alias (.alias p)
        raw-mem (n-in! d MEM-STATE)
        mem (mem-effective raw-mem alias)]
    (if (not (n-same? raw-mem mem))
        (do (n-set-def! d MEM-STATE (Some mem)) (Some d))
        (if (and (= (n-op mem) OP-STORE)
                 (and (= alias (.alias (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr mem))))
                      (and (n-same? (n-in! d MEM-PTR) (n-in! mem MEM-PTR))
                           (n-same? (n-in! d MEM-OFF) (n-in! mem MEM-OFF)))))
            (if (= (n-nouts mem) 1)
                (do (n-set-def! d MEM-STATE (Some (n-in! mem MEM-STATE))) (Some d))
                (do (n-add-dep! mem d) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])))
            (None [(dyn NodeOps)])))))

(impl NodeOps StoreNode
  (hdr [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (ptr NodeHdr)) (primitive/cast (ptr NodeHdr) self))
  (label [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (slice u8)) "Store")
  (is-const? [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (no-const-fold? [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (is-pinned? [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (binop-copy [(self (ptr StoreNode)) (lhs (dyn NodeOps)) (rhs (dyn NodeOps))]
              (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  (compute [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> i64) (store-compute (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (idealize [(self (ptr StoreNode))]
            (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
            (store-idealize (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (eq-extra [(self (ptr StoreNode)) (other (dyn NodeOps))]
            (-> bool)
            (if (!= (n-op other) OP-STORE)
                false
                (let [o (primitive/cast (ptr StoreNode) (hdr other))]
                  (and (= (.alias self) (.alias o)) (= (.declared self) (.declared o))))))
  (hash-extra [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> i64) (^ (* (.alias self) 257) (.declared self))))

(impl MemOps StoreNode
  (mem-node [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self))
  (mem-alias [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> i64) (.alias self))
  (mem-is-load? [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (mem-in [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-STATE))
  (mem-ptr [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-PTR))
  (mem-offset [(self (ptr StoreNode))] (-> (dyn NodeOps)) (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) MEM-OFF)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Load / Store / New
(defn load-make [(ctrl (dyn NodeOps))
                 (mem (dyn NodeOps))
                 (ptr_ (dyn NodeOps))
                 (off (dyn NodeOps))
                 (alias i64)
                 (declared i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        p (alloc/unwrap-ptr [LoadNode] (alloc/create [LoadNode] a))
        d (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps p)]
    (set! (.alias p) alias)
    (set! (.declared p) declared)
    (n-init! d OP-LOAD)
    (n-add-def! d (Some ctrl))
    (n-add-def! d (Some mem))
    (n-add-def! d (Some ptr_))
    (n-add-def! d (Some off))
    (n-set-ty! d (compute p))
    d))

(defn store-make [(ctrl (dyn NodeOps))
                  (mem (dyn NodeOps))
                  (ptr_ (dyn NodeOps))
                  (off (dyn NodeOps))
                  (val (dyn NodeOps))
                  (alias i64)
                  (declared i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        p (alloc/unwrap-ptr [StoreNode] (alloc/create [StoreNode] a))
        d (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps p)]
    (set! (.alias p) alias)
    (set! (.declared p) declared)
    (n-init! d OP-STORE)
    (n-add-def! d (Some ctrl))
    (n-add-def! d (Some mem))
    (n-add-def! d (Some ptr_))
    (n-add-def! d (Some off))
    (n-add-def! d (Some val))
    (n-set-ty! d (compute p))
    d))

;; Final Simple's New is a two-input Multi: control and byte size. JavaScript adds current public
;; memory as input two, because two managed allocations in one control block are observable
;; allocator calls and initialization of the first must precede allocation of the second. Its
;; results are the fresh,
;; non-null pointer at projection zero and private initial memory at projection one. It is not a
;; public-memory transformation: stores that initialize the fresh object consume the private
;; memory result, while the machine node still advertises allocator-call clobbers.
;;
;; `shape` and `object-ty` are deliberately separate. A hidden-class ID belongs to ShapeTable; a
;; struct type belongs to TypeTable. Both happen to be integers, but substituting one namespace for
;; the other would manufacture a pointer whose referent is unrelated to its physical layout.
(defn new-shape [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-NEW)
      (do (panic-i "new-shape: not a New" (n-op n)) 0)
      (.shape (primitive/cast (ptr NewNode) (hdr n)))))

(defn new-object-ty [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-NEW)
      (do (panic-i "new-object-ty: not a New" (n-op n)) TY-BOT)
      (.object-ty (primitive/cast (ptr NewNode) (hdr n)))))

(defn new-size [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-NEW)
      (do (panic-i "new-size: not a New" (n-op n)) (unreachable-node))
      (n-in! n 1)))

(defn new-memory [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (!= (n-op n) OP-NEW)
      (do (panic-i "new-memory: not a New" (n-op n)) (unreachable-node))
      (n-in! n 2)))

(defn new-compute [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [ctrl-ty (n-ty (n-in! n 0))
        object-ty (new-object-ty n)]
    (if (ty-high? ctrl-ty)
        (ty-tuple-of2 TY-TOP TY-TOP)
        (if (= ctrl-ty TY-XCTRL)
            (ty-tuple-of2 TY-TOP TY-TOP)
            (ty-tuple-of2 (ty-memptr false object-ty) (ty-mem-private ALIAS-BULK object-ty))))))

(impl NodeOps NewNode
  (hdr [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> (ptr NodeHdr)) (primitive/cast (ptr NodeHdr) self))
  (label [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> (slice u8)) "New")
  (is-const? [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (no-const-fold? [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (is-pinned? [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (binop-copy [(self (ptr NewNode)) (lhs (dyn NodeOps)) (rhs (dyn NodeOps))]
              (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  (compute [(self (ptr NewNode))]
           (-> i64)
           (new-compute (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (idealize [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps))) (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  ;; Allocation is effectful and every execution returns a distinct identity. Structural equality
  ;; must therefore be false even for equal shape, size, and control operands.
  (eq-extra [(self (ptr NewNode)) (other (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool) (do self other false))
  (hash-extra [(self (ptr NewNode))] (-> i64) (+ (* (.shape self) 271) (.object-ty self))))

(defn new-make [(ctrl (dyn NodeOps))
                (size (dyn NodeOps))
                (mem (dyn NodeOps))
                (shape i64)
                (object-ty i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (do
    (if (not (ty-mem? (n-ty mem))) (n-panic! "new-make: ordering input is not memory" mem) 0)
    (new-make-shell ctrl size mem shape object-ty)))

;; The graph copier's constructor: every input is a placeholder rewired afterwards, so the memory
;; ordering check above does not apply. Shape and object type are still validated.
;; New's inputs: control, byte size, the public memory it allocates in.
(const NEW-MEM 2)

(defn new-make-shell [(ctrl (dyn NodeOps))
                      (size (dyn NodeOps))
                      (mem (dyn NodeOps))
                      (shape i64)
                      (object-ty i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (do
    (if (not (shape-valid? shape)) (panic-i "new-make: invalid hidden-class shape" shape) 0)
    (match (ty-kind object-ty)
      (TStruct [_ _ _ _] 0)
      (_ (panic "new-make: object type is not a struct")))
    (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
          p (alloc/unwrap-ptr [NewNode] (alloc/create [NewNode] a))
          d (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps p)]
      (set! (.shape p) shape)
      (set! (.object-ty p) object-ty)
      (n-init! d OP-NEW)
      (n-add-def! d (Some ctrl))
      (n-add-def! d (Some size))
      (n-add-def! d (Some mem))
      (n-set-ty! d (compute p))
      d)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; MemMerge / ReadOnly
(defn memphi-make [(region (dyn NodeOps)) (alias i64) (elem i64) (name (slice u8))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (< alias ALIAS-BULK)
      (do (panic-i "memphi-make: alias must be positive" alias) (unreachable-node))
      (phi-make-op region (ty-mem alias elem) name OP-MEMPHI)))

(defn memphi-alias [(p (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op p) OP-MEMPHI)
      (do (panic-i "memphi-alias: not a MemPhi" (n-op p)) ALIAS-BULK)
      (ty-mem-alias (phi-declared-ty p))))

(defn memphi-add-state! [(p (dyn NodeOps)) (st (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op p) OP-MEMPHI)
      (panic-i "memphi-add-state!: not a MemPhi" (n-op p))
      (let [st-ty (n-ty st)]
        (if (and (ty-mem? st-ty) (!= (ty-mem-alias st-ty) (memphi-alias p)))
            (panic-i "memphi-add-state!: memory alias mismatch" (ty-mem-alias st-ty))
            (phi-add-value! p st)))))

(defn memphi-open! [(p (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op p) OP-MEMPHI)
      (panic-i "memphi-open!: not a MemPhi" (n-op p))
      (phi-open! p)))

(defn memphi-close! [(p (dyn NodeOps)) (st (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op p) OP-MEMPHI)
      (panic-i "memphi-close!: not a MemPhi" (n-op p))
      (let [st-ty (n-ty st)]
        (if (and (ty-mem? st-ty) (!= (ty-mem-alias st-ty) (memphi-alias p)))
            (panic-i "memphi-close!: memory alias mismatch" (ty-mem-alias st-ty))
            (phi-close! p st)))))

(defn memmerge-compute [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (n-in d 1)
    (Some [mem] (if (ty-mem? (n-ty mem)) (n-ty mem) (if (ty-high? (n-ty mem)) (ty-mem-top 1) (ty-mem 1 TY-BOT))))
    (None [] (ty-mem-top 1))))

(defn memmerge-idealize [(d (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [p (primitive/cast (ptr MemMergeNode) (hdr d))]
    (if (.in-progress p)
        (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
        (match (n-in d 1)
          (None [] (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
          (Some [default]
                (let [(mut i) 2
                      (mut distinct) false
                      (mut changed) false]
                  (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins d))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-in d (load i))
                                (Some [v]
                                      (if (n-same? v default)
                                          (do
                                            (n-set-def! d (load i) (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
                                            (set! (mut changed) true))
                                          (set! (mut distinct) true)))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                              (continue))))
                  (if (not (load distinct))
                      (Some default)
                      (if (load changed) (Some d) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])))))))))

(impl NodeOps MemMergeNode
  (hdr [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> (ptr NodeHdr)) (primitive/cast (ptr NodeHdr) self))
  (label [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> (slice u8)) "MemMerge")
  (is-const? [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (no-const-fold? [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (is-pinned? [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> bool) true)
  (binop-copy [(self (ptr MemMergeNode)) (lhs (dyn NodeOps)) (rhs (dyn NodeOps))]
              (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  (compute [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> i64) (memmerge-compute (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (idealize [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))]
            (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
            (memmerge-idealize (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self)))
  (eq-extra [(self (ptr MemMergeNode)) (other (dyn NodeOps))]
            (-> bool)
            (and (= (n-op other) OP-MEMMERGE) (not (.in-progress self))))
  (hash-extra [(self (ptr MemMergeNode))] (-> i64) 263))

(defn memmerge-make [] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        p (alloc/unwrap-ptr [MemMergeNode] (alloc/create [MemMergeNode] a))
        d (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps p)]
    (set! (.in-progress p) false)
    (n-init! d OP-MEMMERGE)
    (n-add-def! d (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
    (n-add-def! d (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
    (n-set-ty! d (ty-mem-top 1))
    d))

(defn memmerge-alias [(m (dyn NodeOps)) (alias i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (!= (n-op m) OP-MEMMERGE)
      (do (panic-i "memmerge-alias: not a MemMerge" (n-op m)) (unreachable-node))
      (match (if (< alias (n-nins m)) (n-in m alias) (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
        (Some [v] v)
        (None [] (n-in! m 1)))))

(defn memmerge-set-alias! [(m (dyn NodeOps)) (alias i64) (st (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-op m) OP-MEMMERGE)
      (panic-i "memmerge-set-alias!: not a MemMerge" (n-op m))
      (if (< alias 1)
          (panic-i "memmerge-set-alias!: alias must be positive" alias)
          (do
            (n-set-def-x! m alias (Some st))
            ;; Alias one is the default memory and therefore determines the MemMerge's
            ;; public type. This is structural bundle construction, not a pessimistic
            ;; lattice refinement, so replace the constructor seed in either direction.
            (n-force-ty! m (memmerge-compute m))
            (code-add! m)
            0))))

(impl NodeOps ReadOnlyNode
  (hdr [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> (ptr NodeHdr)) (primitive/cast (ptr NodeHdr) self))
  (label [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> (slice u8)) "ReadOnly")
  (is-const? [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (no-const-fold? [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (is-pinned? [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> bool) false)
  (binop-copy [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode)) (lhs (dyn NodeOps)) (rhs (dyn NodeOps))]
              (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
  (compute [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))]
           (-> i64)
           (n-ty (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) 1)))
  (idealize [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))]
            (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
            (let [v (n-in! (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps self) 1)]
              (if (= (n-op v) OP-READONLY) (Some v) (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))))
  (eq-extra [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode)) (other (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool) (= (n-op other) OP-READONLY))
  (hash-extra [(self (ptr ReadOnlyNode))] (-> i64) 269))

(defn readonly-make [(v (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        p (alloc/unwrap-ptr [ReadOnlyNode] (alloc/create [ReadOnlyNode] a))
        d (primitive/make-dyn NodeOps p)]
    (set! (.pad p) 0)
    (n-init! d OP-READONLY)
    (n-add-def! d (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
    (n-add-def! d (Some v))
    (n-set-ty! d (n-ty v))
    d))
